# UI Patterns (Forms, Tables, Search)

Uniform data-entry and data-display interaction patterns.

## Product standards

- Must use shared components from `frontend/lib/shared/` only; check the catalog before creating feature-local widgets ([`components.mdc`](./components.mdc)).
- Must use design tokens exclusively; no hard-coded colors, spacing, or typography ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).
- Must stay fully responsive: mobile list/card fallbacks, desktop tables ([`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc)).
- Must use lazy lists, pagination, and debounced search ([`performance.mdc`](./performance.mdc)).
- Workflows must use hospital language, not internal codes.

## Forms

- Must localize all labels, hints, helper text, and validation messages.
- Field errors beside fields; form-level errors for server/cross-field failures.
- Must prevent duplicate submissions and preserve input on recoverable errors.
- Validation timing: required on blur/submit; format after interaction; map server errors back to fields.

## Lists, tables, pagination

- Must use lazy builders; paginate or server-query large datasets.
- Must not load large tables into memory unnecessarily.
- On mobile, dense tables may become list rows/cards with the same meaning.
- Must localize column labels and use stable item keys.

## Search and filtering

- Must use shared search/select components and debounce remote requests.
- Must show loading, empty, error, and results states clearly.
- Must keep query, filters, and sort explicit in the controller.

## Module workspaces

Queue screens must follow [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc), with permission-gated actions and `human_friendly_id` display, never raw table IDs.

